; Stage 15 B2b negative fixture: `unsafe/cast` is still a reserved spelling.
;
; B2b removed the seven `unsafe/*` whole-string entries from
; `g-special-form-set` — `unsafe` became a real built-in namespace, bound as an
; implicit prefix in every file's environment, and `special-form-named` answers
; for its members by RESOLVING the qualifier and consulting the roster
; (`unsafe-qualified-op`, src/nucleusc.nuc). The reservation must survive that
; move: without it a definer could register a global under the `unsafe/cast`
; key, which the dispatch ladder would then silently shadow forever.
;
; Compiling this must FAIL with:
;   "'unsafe/cast' already names a special form"
(defn unsafe/cast (x:i32):i32
  (return x))

(defn main ():i32
  (return 0))
